    "body": "I see the Attributes: docstring for these in the two classes for some reason do not have the type in them - now it would be int | None I should think. It would be good to add the typehint.\r\n\r\nDo you imagine any cases where users would need to be wary with existing code - if they relied on getting a value back before with None now I imagine code could have problems. We could add an upgrade section and call this aspect out to say users might need to upgrade code using these attributes to now cater to None?",
